  "raw_text": "77\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb102\n):\n \nKing iwaika wina imyula ingnika bara alwani binka nani baku takisa\n \n–\n \nFrom the throne, flashes of lightning and\nsounds of thunder likewise occur\n \n/ Desde el trono, también ocurren destellos de relámpagos y sonidos de truenos)\n\nImyula lipaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto emit flashes of lightning\n \n/ emitir relámpagos\n\nInaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cry, to weep, to moan, to lament, to complain\n \n/ llorar, gemir, lamentarse, quejarse\n\nlnaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \noutcry, crying, weeping, lamentation\n \n/ clamor, llanto, lamentación\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \ndb-Param Marikan 21:4\n \nuses\n \nInanka\n \nto translate\n \nmourning\n \nand\n \nInania lâka\n \nto translate\n \noutcry\n \n/\n \ndb-Param\nMarikan 21: 4\n \nusa\n \nInanka\n \npara traducir\n \nel duelo\n \ne\n \nInania lâka\n \npara traducir\n \nel clamor\n)\n\nInanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmourning, crying, weeping, lamentation\n \n/ duelo, llanto, lamentación\n\nInanka Nani\n \n(\ndb,dba\n,bw\n;\n \nLamentaciones\n-\ndbta\n)\n \n–\n \nLamentations\n \n(Bible book)\n \n/\n \nLamentaciones\n \n(libro bíblico)\n\nIni\n \n(v\n-\npresent participle\n \n/ participle presente\n)\n \n–\n \ncrying, weeping, moaning, lamenting, complaining\n \n/ llorando,\n\ngimiendo, lamentando, quejándose\n\nIni yahwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nYahwi inaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto cry out loud, to weep, to wail, to lament\n \n/ llorar, llorar a gritos, llorar\ndesaforadamente, gemir, lamentarse\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \ndb-Jems4:9\n:\n \nMan nani sari taks, ini yahwi bas\n \n–\n \nBecome sad, weep\n \n/ Entristezcan, lloren)\n\nIndiksan\n \n(\nlv,km\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ninjection\n \n/ inyección\n\nInglis\n \n(adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \nEnglish\n \n/ Inglés, inglesas\n\nIngni\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nlight\n \n/ luz\n\nIngni\n \n(adj-1)\n \n–\n \nbright, clear, shiny, radiant, light\n \n/ brillante, claro, radiante, luz\n\nIngni daukaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nIngwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto light up, to shine, to make bright\n \n/ iluminar, brillar, alumbrar\n\nIngnikira\n \n(adj,adv)\n \n–\n \nbright, clear, shiny, radiant\n \n/ brillante, claro, radiante\n\nIngni\n \n(adj-2)\n \n–\n \nlight, not heavy\n \n/ ligero, no pesado\n\nIngni daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto lighten, to make less heavy\n \n/ aligerar, hacer menos pesado\n\nLapta ingnika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsunlight\n \n/ luz del sol\n\nIngwaia\n \n(v-intrans)\n \n–\n \nto shine, to brighten, to flash, to glow\n \n/ brillar, iluminar, destellar\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nIngni daukaia\n \nis used as the transitive form.\n \nIngkaia is not used /\n \nIngni Daukaia\n \nse utiliza como la forma transitiva.\n\nIngkaia no es usado)\n\nIngwras\n \n(Ingras\n-\ndb\n-\nincorrect spelling /\n \ndb\n-\nortografía incorrecta)\n \n–\n \nnot shining, not glowing\n \n/ no brilla, no esta\n\nbrillando\n\nInipis\n \n–\n \nanyone\n, anybody,\n \nanything, any person,\n \nwhatever,\n \ninsignifican\nt\n \n/ cualquiera, cualquier cosa, cualquier persona,\n\nlo que sea, insignificante\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlv26\n):\n \nJehova ai panika kum pliki taim, upla inipis kum plikras.\n \n–\n \nWhen Jehovah looks for a friend, he doesn’t look for (just)\n\nanybody.\n \n/ Cuando Jehová busca a un amigo, no busca a (solo)\n \ncualquiera\n.\n)\n\nInma\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nshrub, grass, pasture, weed\n \n/ arbusto, hierba, pasto\n\nInma saura\n \n(\ndb\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nweed\n \n/ hierba\n\nInpiksan\n \n(\nlv\n;\n \nImpeksan\n-\ndictu\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ninfection\n \n/ infección\n\nIns\n \n–\n \ninch\n \n/ pulgada\n\nInsaitka\n \n(n/s-construct) (\nkt\n; not in / no en\n \ndict\n,\ndictu\n)\n \n–\n \ninside\n \n/ dentro\n\n(Note/Nota: This word is from the English word inside, but the English word\n \noutside\n \nis not used / Esta palabra proviene de la\npalabra inglesa\n \ninside\n, pero la palabra inglesa\n \noutside\n \nno se usa)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlv36\n):\n \nAi insaitka ra aiklabi ba ai mawan ra param kaikisa.\n \n–\n \nYou can clearly see the internal battle on his face.\n \n/ Puedes ver\nclaramente la batalla interna en su rostro.)\n\nInsal\n \n(Alt:\n \nEnsal\n,\n \nEnsel\n-dict\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nangel\n \n/ ángel\n\nInsal luan yua\n \n(\nlfb,mwb,my\n;\n \nEnsel luan yua\n-\nlrw\n)\n \n–\n \nPassover\n \n/ Pascua\n\nInsal luan yua liliaka\n \n(\ndb,mwb,lfb\n;\n \nEnsal luan yua ba liliaka\n-\ndbta\n)\n \n–\n \nPassover festival\n \n/ Festival de la pascua\n\nInsal saurakira\n \n–\n \nwicked angel, demon\n \n/ ángel malvado, demonio\n\nInsauhkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nInsaukaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto wound, to be wounded\n \n/ herir, ser herido\n\nInsauhkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwound, the wounded\n \n/ herida\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Jirimaya 6:14\n):\n \nupliki nani insauhkanka nani ba\n \n–\n \nthe wounded\n \nof my people\n \n/ la herida de mi pueblo)\n\nInsins\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nIsint\n\nInsis\n \n(a/t:\n \nInjis\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhinge\n \n/ bisagra\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nDur pamaika\n,\n \nDur mihta\n,\n \nWindar pamaika\n,\n \nWindar\nmihta\n)\n\nInska\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfish\n \n/ pescado, pez",
